        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS are delighted to present No. 1 Nottingham Street, North Strand, Dublin 3 to the market, a substantial four-bedroom end-of-terrace red brick property ideally located in one of Dublin's most established and convenient city locations. Extending to c.125 sq.m and dating back to the 1890s, this charming home offers a unique opportunity for both owner occupiers and investors alike.\n\nThe location is truly second to none. Situated in the heart of North Strand, every conceivable amenity is within easy reach including Fairview Park, Clontarf Promenade, East Point Business Park, the IFSC, Croke Park, Connolly Station, and Dublin City Centre itself. A wide selection of shops, cafés, schools, restaurants, and sporting facilities are all close by, while excellent public transport links and easy access to Dublin Airport, the Port Tunnel, and M50 make commuting effortless.\n\nBright and spacious accommodation comprises an entrance hallway, living room to the front, a large kitchen/dining extension to the rear, four generously proportioned bedrooms and five bathrooms, three of which are en-suite. The property offers excellent flexibility and would suit a variety of purchasers seeking a spacious city home or a strong investment opportunity.\n\nNo. 1 comes to the market in good condition throughout and retains plenty of character comparable with homes of this era. Additional benefits include gas fired central heating, double glazed windows, generous room proportions, and excellent natural light throughout. To the rear is a private low-maintenance courtyard with a block-built storage unit offering additional practicality.\n\nEarly viewing is highly advised. Contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers today to arrange a viewing.\n \nKey Features\n\n<ul>\n <li>c.125 sq.m</li>\n <li>BER D</li>\n <li>Spacious 4-bedroom end-of-terrace property</li>\n <li>5 bathrooms including 3 en-suite bathrooms</li>\n <li>Attractive red brick home dating from the 1890s</li>\n <li>Gas fired central heating</li>\n <li>Double glazed windows throughout</li>\n <li>Large kitchen/dining extension</li>\n <li>Bright and spacious accommodation</li>\n <li>Generous room proportions throughout</li>\n <li>Private rear courtyard</li>\n <li>Block-built unit to rear</li>\n <li>Excellent rental potential</li>\n <li>Walking distance to Dublin City Centre</li>\n <li>Close to Fairview Park, Clontarf, IFSC & East Point Business Park</li>\n <li>Excellent public transport links nearby</li>\n <li>Easy access to Dublin Airport, Port Tunnel & M50</li>\n <li>Ideal for investors and owner occupiers alike</li>\n <li>Viewing highly advised</li>\n</ul>"
      },
      {
